<article class="env-definition" id="035H">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/035H">Definition <span data-tag="035H">29.54.3</span>.</a> Let $f : Y \to X$ be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated morphism of schemes. Let $\mathcal{O}'$ be the integral closure of $\mathcal{O}_ X$ in $f_*\mathcal{O}_ Y$. The <em>normalization of $X$ in $Y$</em> is the scheme<a class="footnotemark" href="#a0000660787" id="a0000660787-mark"><sup>1</sup></a> </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \nu : X' = \underline{\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}}_ X(\mathcal{O}') \to X  \]
</div>
  <p> over $X$. It comes equipped with a natural factorization </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  Y \xrightarrow {f'} X' \xrightarrow {\nu } X  \]
</div>
  <p> of the initial morphism $f$. </p>
</article>